{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1795215873,"nonce":"UwQXrjDpFGggD6aVnfJwNo5SODU=","message":"Correction and breakdown of the x86 gap.\n\nThe previous comment blamed the gap on Immix ignoring explicit releases. That is wrong for the churn rows: w_phase makes 198M small allocations and 19 frees in the whole run, so both heaps reclaim everything by collection.\n\nCollection counts are the same under both heaps: w_phase 231, Python binary_trees 42, Lua binary_trees 15, w_hold 6, w_grow 2. tok2 differs, with 22 collections for Immix against 26 for the pool and a larger mean live set at collection (44 MB against 37 MB).\n\nWhere the time goes (NUC, x86_64):\n- Churn rows: collection time is level. w_phase 154 ms against 113 ms, Python binary_trees 91 ms against 93 ms. The gap is in allocation, on the mutator side.\n- Zeroing: Immix memsets every recycled region (7.3 GB, 470 ms in w_phase). The pool never zeroes blocks and clears only the last 16 bytes of a slot. Skipping the region memset and clearing only the slack past each request recovered 0.42 s of the 1.16 s gap on w_phase, 0.16 s of 0.76 s on w_hold, 0.12 s of 0.60 s on tok2 and almost nothing on Lua binary_trees. The HostHeap contract says alloc returns zeroed memory, but the pool does not, so the runtime cannot rely on it. Landing this needs a contract change and the full suite under Immix.\n- Large live sets: marking is the slow part, not the sweep. tok2 marks for 517 ms over 22 collections against 202 ms total for the pool over 26. w_hold marks for 722 ms against 601 ms total for the pool at an equal 331 MB live set. w_grow is level.\n- What is left on w_phase once zeroing is gone is about 0.74 s over 198M allocations (3.7 ns each): the call through the table, the thread-local region and the start-byte store.\n- A smaller collection floor does not help. Floors of 2 to 16 MB leave tok2 flat, change w_phase by less than the run-to-run noise, and make Lua binary_trees slower (0.22 s to 0.29 s) through extra collections.\n\nNext in order of payoff: drop the region zeroing, shorten the mark loop (the byte-per-quantum start table is walked for every candidate word), then the allocation fast path.","files":null}]}